Description: Detects linkage-disequilibrium blocks and supports haplotype
    analysis, genomic prediction, multivariate and genotype-by-environment
    prediction, parent selection, optimum-contribution selection, genomic
    mating, operational plan certification, interoperable recommendation
    export, and core-collection design. Compiled routines
    calculate standard r-squared and kinship-adjusted rV-squared statistics.
    Input readers support dosage tables, HapMap, VCF, GDS, and PLINK BED
    files; memory use depends on the source format and selected backend.
    Breeder-facing methods return quality-control, provenance, validation,
    and uncertainty information where it can be estimated. Beagle phasing
    is supported through an explicitly configured external Beagle 5.x JAR.
    Dosage-based relationship and marker-effect calculations can accept
    alternative ploidy values, but haplotype inference, phased
    representations, and compiled LD kernels currently assume diploid,
    biallelic data.
